## 2149. Rearrange Array Elements by Sign

### Approach - 1

1. Traverse the array and separate positive and negative numbers into two arrays while maintaining their original order.
2. Since the result must start with a positive number and alternate signs, place positive numbers at even indices and negative numbers at odd indices.
3. Use separate pointers for the positive and negative arrays to fill the result.
4. Return the rearranged array.

Time Complexity : O(n)
Space Complexity : O(n), Uses extra 2 arrays

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public int[] rearrangeArray(int[] nums) {
        int[] pos = new int[nums.length / 2];
        int[] neg = new int[nums.length / 2];
        int posIndex = 0;
        int negIndex = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            if (nums[i] > 0) {
                pos[posIndex++] = nums[i];
            } else {
                neg[negIndex++] = nums[i];
            }
        }
        posIndex = 0;
        negIndex = 0;
        int[] res = new int[nums.length];
        for (int i = 0; i < res.length; i++) {
            if (i % 2 == 0) {
                res[i] = pos[posIndex++];
            } else {
                res[i] = neg[negIndex++];
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}


### Approach - 2 (Optimal)

1. Create a result array of the same size as nums.
2. Maintain two pointers:
--  pos = 0 → next position for a positive number.
--  neg = 1 → next position for a negative number.
3. Traverse nums:
--  If the number is positive, place it at pos and increase pos by 2.
--  If the number is negative, place it at neg and increase neg by 2.
4. Return the result array.

Time Complexity : O(n)
Space Complexity :  O(n)

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {
    public int[] rearrangeArray(int[] nums) {
        int posIndex = 0; // it goes Even range 0-2-4-6 
        int negIndex = 1; // it goes Odd rage 1-3-5-7
        int[] res = new int[nums.length];
        for (int num : nums) {
            if (num > 0) {
                res[posIndex] = num;
                posIndex += 2;
            } else {
                res[negIndex] = num;
                negIndex += 2;
            }
        }
        return res;
    }
}
